# Shepherd Implementation Plan

This document outlines the implementation tasks for the Shepherd project, based on the provided documentation. Tasks are organized into phases.

If something has - [x] an x it means it has be done please ignore. 

## Phase 1: Project Setup & Core UI Foundation

- [x] **Environment Setup:** Initialize React Native/Expo project with TypeScript (if not already done). *Reference: `project_requirements_document.mdc`, `tech_stack_document.mdc`*
- [x] **Install Core Dependencies:** Add Nativewind, Expo Router, Zustand, Rive, and Firebase SDKs. *Reference: `tech_stack_document.mdc`*
- [x] **Basic File Structure:** Set up initial directory structure (`app/`, `components/`, `assets/`, `store/`, `services/`, etc.). *Reference: `cursor_project_rules.mdc`*
- [x] **Expo Router Configuration:** Set up basic Tab Bar navigation layout (`app/_layout.tsx`) with placeholder screens for core sections (e.g., Home, Map, Bible, Stats, Profile). *Reference: `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`, `app_flow_document.mdc`, `app_flowchart.mdc`*
- [x] **Nativewind Setup:** Configure Nativewind for styling. *Reference: `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`*
- [x] **Font Integration:**
    - [x] Configure `tailwind.config.js` to include custom fonts ('Feather Bold', 'DIN Next Rounded LT W01 Regular') from `assets/fonts/`. *Reference: User request, `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`*
    - [x] Load fonts in the app entry point (`app/_layout.tsx` or similar).
- [ ] **Home Screen UI:**
    - [ ] Create `app/home/screen.tsx` (or similar based on router structure).
    - [ ] Implement the two-section layout described in `app_flow_document.mdc`.
    - [ ] Integrate the Rive animation component (`rive-react-native`) in the top section. *Reference: User request, `project_requirements_document.mdc`, `tech_stack_document.mdc`*
    - [ ] Style the screen similar to the provided `@exampleHomeUI` reference, using Nativewind and the defined color palette/fonts. *Reference: User request, `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`*
    - [ ] Add placeholder buttons for Bible Reading, Prayer, and Reflection in the lower section.

## Phase 2: Onboarding & Authentication

- [ ] **Create Onboarding Screens:** Develop individual screens for the onboarding flow as outlined in `app_flow_document.mdc` and `project_requirements_document.mdc` (Welcome, Name Lamb, Denomination, Goal, Experience, Frequency). Place them in `app/onboarding/` or similar.
- [ ] **Implement Onboarding Navigation:** Set up navigation flow between onboarding screens using Expo Router.
- [ ] **Firebase Setup (Backend):** Create Firebase project, enable Firestore and Authentication (Anonymous, SIWA, Google). *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Firebase Integration (Frontend):** Add Firebase configuration to the app.
- [ ] **Implement Authentication Screens:** Create screens for Sign-Up/Sign-In/Password Recovery. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Implement Authentication Logic:** Connect sign-up/sign-in screens to Firebase Auth (Anonymous, SIWA, Google). *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc`, `tech_stack_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Connect Onboarding to Auth:** Save onboarding choices to Firestore upon account creation/sign-in. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Users Collection)*
- [ ] **State Management (Auth):** Use Zustand to manage user authentication state globally. *Reference: `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`*

## Phase 3: Core Features Implementation

- [ ] **Bible API Service:** Create a modular service (`services/bibleService.ts`) to interact with the chosen Bible API. Implement basic fetching. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc`, `tech_stack_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Bible Content Caching:** Implement local caching for Bible content using Zustand and Async Storage for offline access. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc`, `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`, `project_requirements_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Bible Reading Screen:** Develop the UI for the daily Bible reading session, including fetching verses via `bibleService` and displaying content. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Reading Progress Tracking:** Save reading progress to Firestore and update local state. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Activity Logs/Users Collection)*
- [ ] **Reflection/Journaling:**
    - [ ] Create the Reflection/Journaling screen UI. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
    - [ ] Implement logic to save journal entries to Firestore. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Activity Logs/Users Collection)*
- [ ] **Guided Prayer:**
    - [ ] Design and implement the UI for different prayer modes (Quick, ACTS, Lord's Prayer) potentially using swipeable cards. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
    - [ ] Implement logic to track prayer session completion in Firestore. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Activity Logs/Users Collection)*
- [ ] **Bible Study Path/Map Screen:** Create the basic UI for the Duolingo-style map interface (visual representation, path structure). *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`, `project_requirements_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Gamification Data Models:** Define Firestore structures for streaks, XP. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Users Collection)*
- [ ] **Update Gamification Metrics:** Implement logic to update streaks/XP in Firestore after completing activities (reading, prayer).
- [ ] **Display Gamification Metrics:** Show streak/XP data on the Home screen. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*

## Phase 4: Settings, Monetization & Refinement

- [ ] **Settings Screen UI:** Develop the UI for the settings page. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Implement Settings Logic:** Allow users to update profile details, notification preferences (placeholders for now), and view Bible version choice. Save changes to Firestore. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Users Collection)*
- [ ] **RevenueCat/Superwall Setup:** Integrate RevenueCat and Superwall SDKs. Configure products/paywalls. *Reference: `tech_stack_document.mdc`, `project_requirements_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Pricing Page UI:** Create the UI for the subscription/pricing page. *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **Implement Subscription Logic:** Connect UI to RevenueCat/Superwall to handle purchases and check subscription status. Update user status in Firestore. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc` (Users/Monetization Collection)*
- [ ] **Pro Feature Gates:** Implement logic to conditionally show/hide or disable features based on subscription status.
- [ ] **Error Handling:** Implement user-friendly error messages for common issues (network, invalid input, API errors). *Reference: `app_flow_document.mdc`*
- [ ] **UI Polishing:** Refine animations, transitions, and overall visual consistency based on `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`.
- [ ] **Testing:** Conduct thorough testing (unit, integration, E2E) across different devices/platforms. *Reference: `frontend_guidelines_document.mdc`*

## Phase 5: Deployment

- [ ] **Build Preparation:** Configure app builds for iOS and Android using Expo Application Services (EAS).
- [ ] **Final Testing:** Perform final QA and beta testing.
- [ ] **App Store/Play Store Submission:** Prepare metadata and submit the app.
- [ ] **Monitoring Setup:** Configure Firebase monitoring (Crashlytics, Performance) for the production app. *Reference: `backend_structure_document.mdc`*

---

*This plan is iterative. Task priorities may shift based on development progress and feedback.*
